
==============================================================================
[2] does the verdict track the arm it should?
==============================================================================

  arm                              U called determined   median U error
  state mask + plume|test_id                       88 %             0.7 %
  state mask + plume|test_ood                      72 %             0.8 %
  state mask only|test_id                          17 %            26.8 %

  Wind speed is algebraically undetermined from masks alone (section 1) and
  well determined with the plume (section 9). The guard is asked to say so
  without being told which arm it is looking at.

==============================================================================
[3] are the intervals honest?
==============================================================================

  A 1-sigma interval should contain the truth about 68 % of the time. Cases
  where the inversion converged badly are counted separately, because an
  interval around the wrong point says nothing about the interval's width.

  arm                             n determined   median sigma   truth inside   converged only
  state mask + plume|test_id                22          0.52 %            55 %              57 %
  state mask + plume|test_ood               18          0.43 %            61 %              67 %
  state mask only|test_id                    2          1.68 %             0 %             nan %

  Pooled over the converged cases: 22 of 36 = 61 %, 95 % interval 43-77 %.
  The nominal 68 % is inside that interval, so these intervals are consistent with being honest;
  36 cases cannot resolve better than that. The point estimate is low, and scaling sigma by 1.06 would land it exactly on 68 %.

==============================================================================
[4] the guard against the residual check, on the same cases
==============================================================================

  62 inversions, 25 of them wrong by more than 5 % on wind speed

         raised by   wrong, caught   wrong, missed   right, flagged
    residual check              10              15                2
     profile guard              19               6                1
            either              21               4                2

  The residual check catches 10 of 25 and misses 15; the profile guard catches 19 and misses 6.
  They fail on different cases, which is the point: a wrong answer that fits
  the data perfectly is invisible to the first and obvious to the second.
